   "titulo": "Type of housing and rooms",
   "texto": [
    "In Norwegian, in and et go in front of the noun: in leilighet, et hus. In Bokmål, many words feminine also admit in.",
    "For the defined form, the article is added at the end: et hus → hustet; in leilighet → leiligheten. In Spanish, «the / the» goes ahead; in Norwegian it is often linked to the noun.",
    "Den means «the» or «That one.» when it refers to a thing of common gender, as in leilighett. Det is used with a neutral noun."
   ]
